  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f53996727138b9442ac041cf492618db8287b54ba652c4f9e375cdde27dc1862.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $34{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $\u25b3BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by finding the area of $\u25b3ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\u25b3ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{52}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =67.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{52}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =53.190\u2026 \\\\  & \u224853{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $\u25b3ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $\u25b3BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\u25b3BCD} & ={A}_{\u25b3ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =53-34 \\\\  & =19{\\text{\u00a0cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
